   "evidence": "The temporary test persisted two rows carrying future GitHub waits: a queued row with error \"cancelled by tester\" and a cancelled row with the same mark. It closed and reopened the factory and started its scheduler; neither row was reconciled. HEAD startup reads only status: [\"running\", \"waiting_input\"] at scheduler.ts:31. Queue selection additionally requires githubWait.nextAttemptAt <= now in store.ts:1808, so the queued row cannot reach the cancellation helper until due; cancelled rows never reach it. Base has the same narrow startup recovery filter, but lacks the new future-retry exclusion and GitHub wait state. This exposes a recovery omission through the new waiting behavior. The due-time guard at scheduler.ts:127 still prevents delivery, so the demonstrated consequence is delayed terminal bookkeeping and stale metadata, not execution after restart."
